# Vendor binaries are deliberately not redistributed.
#
# Shadow Defender is commercial software. Copies of its executables and driver
# must not be published, so the binaries taken from the analysis host are kept
# out of this repository. The analysis is reproducible from the installation
# itself: copy the files back into samples/ (see README.md §2 for the list) and
# run the toolchain. Every relevant hash is recorded in README.md §8 and
# recon/verification.md (V5) so the correct inputs can be confirmed.
samples/*.exe
samples/*.dll
samples/*.sys

# Working copies of the above, used by the unhide script.
work/

# IDA databases are large machine-local artifacts and are regenerated on demand.
*.i64
*.idb
*.til

# Python bytecode cache from the tools.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# This installation's own settings file: contains the licence serial (obfuscated
# but trivially decodable). Deliberately not published. Recreate by copying the
# file from the analysed installation if you need to follow the worked example
# in docs/07-config-and-formats.md.
samples/user.dat

# The vendor's installation package (contains the signed commercial binaries).
# Not redistributed. See docs/10-installer.md for the analysis; the payload can
# be recreated from a copy of the supplied package.
安装包/
